WEBVTT

00:27.961 --> 00:32.032
(Azure Spring)

00:32.032 --> 00:34.501
(All characters, places, events, etc. depicted are fictional.)

00:34.501 --> 00:36.970
(Children and animals were filmed under strict guidelines.)

02:12.399 --> 02:13.467
And they're off!

02:13.467 --> 02:16.336
A nice, clean entry by Han Ye Gyeong from Korea.

02:16.670 --> 02:18.105
She's now above the surface...

02:18.105 --> 02:19.773
and begins her freestyle stroke.

02:20.440 --> 02:22.442
She's got a smooth arm rotation and a steady rhythm.

02:22.709 --> 02:25.546
She's already approaching the turn.

02:26.547 --> 02:28.081
And she turns!

02:28.682 --> 02:30.717
Excellent! A perfect touch on the wall...

02:30.717 --> 02:32.019
and a seamless turn.

02:32.019 --> 02:34.021
She accelerates again effortlessly.

02:34.254 --> 02:36.757
Now, heading for the final 10m push.

02:36.957 --> 02:39.126
Han Ye Gyeong!

02:39.126 --> 02:42.262
And she touches! She comes in first!

02:42.529 --> 02:44.798
She wins a gold medal!

02:45.499 --> 02:46.600
It's an unbelievable moment.

02:46.600 --> 02:50.370
Korean women's swimming finally captures another gold.

02:50.604 --> 02:52.739
A new dark horse emerges!

02:52.739 --> 02:55.542
Han Ye Gyeong finally did it!

02:55.709 --> 02:59.112
Thank you for watching. We're proud of you, Han!

02:59.213 --> 03:02.349
We have now entered Han Ye Gyeong's era!

03:02.349 --> 03:04.017
(Han Ye Gyeong debuts with a gold medal)

03:04.017 --> 03:05.719
Dreams do come true.

03:06.520 --> 03:08.789
(Han Ye Gyeong Breaks South Korean Women's Swimming Record)

03:11.425 --> 03:12.426
But of course,

03:13.260 --> 03:15.195
it's not necessarily mine.

04:33.173 --> 04:34.575
"Beautiful waves."

04:35.676 --> 04:37.644
That's what the name Parang-ri means.

04:38.078 --> 04:39.379
It's famous for its sun glitter,

04:39.646 --> 04:41.348
even in Namhae, where islands are abundant.

04:44.985 --> 04:48.388
It's a remote town across the sea, an hour by boat from Tongyeong...

04:48.388 --> 04:49.790
where the mainland ends.

04:54.728 --> 04:55.729
This is...

04:56.563 --> 04:57.564
my hometown.

05:33.867 --> 05:34.868
That was rough.

06:12.873 --> 06:14.141
It's been five years already.

06:14.942 --> 06:16.076
Why is this place so clean?

06:17.678 --> 06:19.313
I won't have to clean out the whole place.

08:13.227 --> 08:16.063
My mom never used the iron cauldron.

08:16.897 --> 08:20.000
She spent the whole day hauling in dozens of seafood,

08:20.801 --> 08:23.036
so she dreaded the idea of coming home...

08:23.470 --> 08:26.840
and having to lift the heavy cauldron...

08:27.474 --> 08:28.575
to wash and cook.

08:38.418 --> 08:39.887
But once a year, on my birthday,

08:40.220 --> 08:43.891
she'd throw in lots of sea mustard she harvested on that day...

08:43.891 --> 08:45.259
into this cauldron to make me soup.

09:07.681 --> 09:08.682
How odd.

09:09.149 --> 09:10.584
I return home after so long,

09:11.585 --> 09:14.354
and of all things, I'm making seaweed soup in this very cauldron.

09:16.690 --> 09:17.691
Seo An Na,

09:18.058 --> 09:19.059
happy birthday.

10:04.938 --> 10:06.740
It may not be such a bad idea...

10:07.641 --> 10:09.076
to live in hiding like this.

10:34.368 --> 10:35.502
He's that kid.

10:36.570 --> 10:38.205
I mentioned him to you once before.

10:41.441 --> 10:42.843
Come on.

10:43.210 --> 10:44.745
(Parang-ri Fishing Cooperative, Community Center)

10:44.745 --> 10:45.746
Where is it?

10:46.380 --> 10:48.415
Here. Look.

10:50.284 --> 10:52.519
Good job today.

10:53.754 --> 10:55.689
There's a kid looking for a place to stay.

10:55.689 --> 10:57.457
Can I rent out your mother's place?

10:57.457 --> 10:58.926
(Parang-ri Village Chief)

10:58.926 --> 11:00.360
Let him live there for free.

11:00.360 --> 11:02.896
It's empty, anyway. It'd be nice to keep a person around.

11:02.896 --> 11:04.665
(Parang-ri Village Chief)

11:04.665 --> 11:06.433
(It'd be nice to keep a person around.)

11:08.836 --> 11:09.837
See?

11:10.904 --> 11:12.239
Are you staying for long, An Na?

11:14.441 --> 11:15.542
Did you quit swimming?

11:15.542 --> 11:17.511
What do you mean? I haven't quit.

11:17.511 --> 11:19.246
Why are you getting mad at me?

11:20.080 --> 11:24.484
If you're hanging out for a few days, you two can stay together.

11:25.085 --> 11:26.620
It's not the Joseon era anymore,

11:26.854 --> 11:28.388
and you have lots of rooms.

11:28.388 --> 11:29.423
Chief.

11:30.090 --> 11:31.959
He's not a scary guy.

11:33.360 --> 11:34.528
That's a cold stare.

11:35.629 --> 11:38.098
Anyway, you young ones...

11:38.098 --> 11:41.602
should talk it out and reach an agreement.

11:42.369 --> 11:44.771
How nice. You look good together.

11:45.706 --> 11:47.808
Something is about to happen, don't you think?

11:53.981 --> 11:55.215
Since it's come to this,

11:56.283 --> 11:57.818
let's live together and make it work.

11:59.353 --> 12:01.688
Mr. Tenant, you can use the guest room, and I, the back room.

12:01.889 --> 12:04.124
We just won't bother each other.

12:04.391 --> 12:06.159
We'll pretend like we don't hear each other's calls,

12:06.159 --> 12:07.961
and we won't watch what each other eats.

12:08.328 --> 12:10.731
We may live together, but it'll be like we're alone.

12:11.532 --> 12:12.599
Any thoughts, Mr. Tenant?

12:17.804 --> 12:20.274
Hey, why aren't you saying anything?

12:21.074 --> 12:24.778
Are you willing to cooperate or not?

12:25.245 --> 12:26.346
Will you be staying for a while?

12:28.115 --> 12:30.150
Why are you and the chief asking the same thing?

12:30.150 --> 12:31.985
Why do you need to know how long I'm staying?

12:32.519 --> 12:34.855
I'm staying for a very long time,

12:35.255 --> 12:36.256
until the day I die.

12:36.557 --> 12:37.925
I hope you do.

12:41.628 --> 12:42.930
Did he completely disregard me?

12:44.498 --> 12:46.500
Hey! You!

12:51.271 --> 12:52.272
Hey!

12:53.640 --> 12:54.641
An Na!

12:55.375 --> 12:56.410
It's you, right?

12:56.944 --> 12:58.045
Who are you?

12:58.846 --> 13:00.247
It really is you!

13:00.547 --> 13:03.450
Parang-ri Mermaid, Seo An Na!

13:04.785 --> 13:06.286
It's been so long!

13:06.520 --> 13:07.821
Merm... What?

13:09.489 --> 13:11.325
Do you recognise me?

13:13.827 --> 13:16.330
It's me, Parang-ri Trot Goddess,

13:16.663 --> 13:18.432
Baek Su Jeong.

13:18.832 --> 13:22.236
Oh my, oh my, don't do this

13:22.836 --> 13:26.874
Women's feelings are quite fickle

13:27.074 --> 13:30.777
No, don't do this, and don't ask

13:31.245 --> 13:35.816
You can't ask for more from me

13:36.950 --> 13:40.654
Today is the first time I met you

13:46.660 --> 13:48.929
Parang-ri Trot Goddess is performing,

13:48.929 --> 13:50.531
so how dare you try to run away?

13:50.531 --> 13:51.765
Sorry.

13:52.633 --> 13:54.835
I have to go to my swim practice.

13:55.602 --> 13:57.771
I can't stop Parang Mermaid from her swim practice.

13:58.205 --> 13:59.907
Have a good practice. Keep it up!

14:00.240 --> 14:01.308
Okay. Bye.

14:03.243 --> 14:05.179
Now, focus. I'm starting over.

14:06.079 --> 14:09.583
Oh my, oh my, don't do this

14:12.653 --> 14:14.621
Gosh. I'm done.

14:17.191 --> 14:18.892
I'm done living alone.

14:19.593 --> 14:22.262
As they say, a singer's voice is what defines her.

14:22.462 --> 14:24.798
You remembered right away as soon as you heard me sing.

14:25.999 --> 14:27.167
I knew that'd be the case.

14:27.768 --> 14:29.570
And I'm done living a quiet life.

14:30.037 --> 14:31.104
Anyway,

14:31.305 --> 14:32.906
I thought you became a swimmer in Seoul.

14:33.273 --> 14:34.408
Why did you suddenly return?

14:36.210 --> 14:38.178
Well, the thing is...

14:38.812 --> 14:40.647
Actually, the Parang-ri Mermaid who left...

14:40.848 --> 14:42.482
to become a swimmer in Seoul...

14:53.139 --> 14:54.407
Hey, there.

14:54.661 --> 14:56.730
You've been looking exhausted lately.

14:57.069 --> 14:59.639
Your boyfriend must be a stunner at night.

15:01.359 --> 15:04.772
- What? - Your boyfriend must be pretty intense.

15:04.817 --> 15:05.918
Keep cleaning up.

15:09.676 --> 15:11.445
Mermaid, my foot.

15:13.447 --> 15:14.982
I was no longer...

15:15.616 --> 15:16.783
the Parang-ri Mermaid.

15:22.523 --> 15:24.758
Hey, stop. Right there. Stay still. Do not move.

15:25.292 --> 15:26.426
Hey, don't move.

15:27.294 --> 15:28.695
You know what?

15:30.330 --> 15:32.432
Your butts are looking great today.

15:32.866 --> 15:36.036
Anyone who passes you by and brushes past those...

15:36.236 --> 15:37.938
will get hard right away.

15:38.972 --> 15:40.007
You punk!

15:42.843 --> 15:45.179
Hey, did you call me a punk?

15:45.379 --> 15:47.848
Yes, I called you a punk. So what, you pervert?

15:47.848 --> 15:50.083
- I'll kill you! - An Na!

15:50.817 --> 15:53.387
I'm letting you off easy today.

15:53.387 --> 15:55.722
Darn it. I've had enough!

15:56.957 --> 15:58.358
I got a nosebleed!

15:58.825 --> 16:00.394
Look at this!

16:00.394 --> 16:01.562
Hey, Seo An Na!

16:01.962 --> 16:04.398
Don't come in starting tomorrow!

16:06.200 --> 16:07.835
You're fired!

16:25.986 --> 16:27.888
It had been a while since I last swam.

16:28.789 --> 16:30.691
I had a job at a swimming pool but got fired.

16:34.187 --> 16:36.690
There's no need to share this story with Su Jeong,

16:37.264 --> 16:38.866
the village bigmouth.

16:39.399 --> 16:41.502
So, why are you here?

16:42.436 --> 16:45.272
Why did you return?

16:45.873 --> 16:46.874
No reason.

16:48.075 --> 16:49.710
- It just felt unfair. - Unfair?

16:50.878 --> 16:51.879
What felt unfair?

16:52.813 --> 16:53.914
Anyway,

16:54.348 --> 16:56.483
about that guy who lives at my place.

16:56.483 --> 16:58.285
You mean my dear Duk Hyun?

16:59.686 --> 17:00.687
Your dear?

17:01.355 --> 17:04.591
Anyway, what does he do?

17:06.226 --> 17:07.394
He's a haenam.

17:07.694 --> 17:08.929
- Haenam? A freediver? - Yes.

17:09.329 --> 17:11.798
He free dives to harvest seafood.

17:13.233 --> 17:15.068
And he makes it look so cool.

17:28.115 --> 17:30.384
Nice job, Duk Hyun!

17:33.287 --> 17:36.356
This place is a bit of a climb,

17:36.690 --> 17:38.625
but the rooms are pretty nice.

17:39.259 --> 17:41.962
Goodness. How nice. This is great.

17:44.731 --> 17:46.166
This place has...

17:46.867 --> 17:48.702
a great view.

17:49.736 --> 17:51.271
His name is Yoon Duk Hyun.

17:51.271 --> 17:52.940
His age, occupation, and past...

17:53.674 --> 17:55.008
Unknown.

17:55.008 --> 17:57.978
One day, he literally...

17:58.979 --> 18:01.715
flew in like the wind...

18:01.748 --> 18:03.750
as a mysterious young man.

18:05.652 --> 18:06.720
Wait a second.

18:07.187 --> 18:08.222
No.

18:09.289 --> 18:11.325
Are you interested in him, too?

18:11.625 --> 18:12.626
"Too"?

18:15.529 --> 18:17.898
Wait, are you into him?

18:19.733 --> 18:21.034
You tell me first.

18:21.201 --> 18:22.936
I thought you were staying only for a few days.

18:22.936 --> 18:24.404
Aren't you going to swim again?

18:24.404 --> 18:26.173
I am. I will do it.

18:26.406 --> 18:27.941
Why are you pestering me, too?

18:28.609 --> 18:30.811
And I'm not interested.

18:32.246 --> 18:33.714
What do you see in that rude guy?

18:34.381 --> 18:36.383
What do you mean, "rude"?

18:36.984 --> 18:39.586
He's a mysterious, young male freediver.

18:40.454 --> 18:42.356
Isn't it almost too sexy?

18:44.458 --> 18:45.559
"Sexy"?

19:11.385 --> 19:13.387
How is that guy sexy?

19:13.387 --> 19:14.721
He's just tanned, that's all.

19:17.991 --> 19:20.060
Hey, you caught a sea bream.

19:20.260 --> 19:21.795
That'll make a delicious soup.

19:21.995 --> 19:25.265
Weren't we going to ignore what each other was eating?

19:28.468 --> 19:30.704
I was just commenting.

19:31.772 --> 19:34.208
Sea breams are delicious when they're made into soup.

19:35.142 --> 19:36.176
I'm just sharing information!

19:45.953 --> 19:47.187
He's sexy, all right.

19:47.855 --> 19:49.423
If you think a tanned jerk is sexy.

19:52.025 --> 19:53.160
What's with him?

20:17.985 --> 20:19.486
I'm in the middle of nowhere,

20:20.153 --> 20:22.256
where food is the only enjoyment available.

20:25.559 --> 20:26.760
Pull yourself together, An Na.

20:27.361 --> 20:28.896
He wouldn't share even if you asked.

20:29.162 --> 20:30.497
Where's your pride?

20:44.678 --> 20:45.679
I know.

21:10.404 --> 21:14.741
(General Store)

21:14.741 --> 21:16.410
How come the general store closes at 7pm?

21:29.923 --> 21:32.626
Why won't you pick up? Did you block my number?

21:33.660 --> 21:36.263
Don't you know that the owner has ties to the association?

21:36.263 --> 21:37.364
(Do Not Answer)

21:37.364 --> 21:39.366
Are you going to quit swimming forever?

21:50.077 --> 21:51.512
That used to glitter so brightly,

21:52.880 --> 21:54.281
but now it's pitch black.

21:55.516 --> 21:58.385
It's so dark I wouldn't even recognise a ghost if I saw one.

22:20.274 --> 22:21.775
Gosh, I'm starving.

22:42.930 --> 22:43.931
Mr. Tenant!

22:45.866 --> 22:46.867
Are you around?

22:51.672 --> 22:52.673
Is he not here?

22:54.308 --> 22:55.742
Excuse me!

23:01.048 --> 23:02.149
You aren't here, are you?

23:10.224 --> 23:11.725
Look how neat he is.

23:12.526 --> 23:13.794
It must be his personality.

23:21.368 --> 23:23.537
Where could he have hidden it?

23:34.214 --> 23:36.884
I knew it. I instinctively know where I can find food.

23:48.161 --> 23:49.162
Sea squirts?

23:49.796 --> 23:51.532
Why did he freeze these delicious things?

23:51.965 --> 23:53.834
He should've mixed it with rice and finished it.

23:54.568 --> 23:57.171
Oh, well, I guess I'll eat these.

24:00.207 --> 24:02.876
(Parang-ri)

24:02.876 --> 24:04.545
Chief, can I steal from your field?

24:04.545 --> 24:05.879
Sure. Go ahead.

25:01.602 --> 25:03.036
A warm clear fish soup...

25:03.237 --> 25:05.906
is the best kind of breakfast that's easy on the stomach.

25:08.942 --> 25:11.812
If the fish used to make the soup is blowfish, it's blowfish soup.

25:12.212 --> 25:14.882
And if it's baby sea bream like I'm using right now,

25:14.882 --> 25:16.383
it becomes sea bream soup.

25:50.417 --> 25:53.353
It's a given that you eat sea squirt when it's freshly caught,

25:53.353 --> 25:55.656
mixed with white rice, lettuce, and sesame oil.

25:56.957 --> 25:58.525
But even after you miss the golden time,

25:59.026 --> 26:01.762
it can still become a delicacy if you turn it into jeon.

26:18.812 --> 26:21.048
When the ingredient doesn't look too promising,

26:21.048 --> 26:22.549
return to rule one of living alone.

26:26.353 --> 26:27.487
Cook it in oil.

27:34.121 --> 27:36.256
Gosh. I should...

27:37.791 --> 27:38.959
return, right?

27:49.102 --> 27:51.405
Does sharing the kitchen include the food?

27:52.406 --> 27:53.407
You startled me.

27:57.344 --> 27:58.345
Well, it seemed like...

27:58.846 --> 28:00.147
you discarded these.

28:01.114 --> 28:04.484
In that case, you would've found it in the trash can, not the fridge.

28:06.820 --> 28:09.756
Don't be so cheap. All I had were leftover fish heads and sea squirts.

28:10.023 --> 28:12.025
Do you think it's easy to harvest sea squirts?

28:12.793 --> 28:14.595
What a show off, just because you can catch some seafood.

28:15.662 --> 28:17.898
I wasn't a bad swimmer myself.

28:18.332 --> 28:20.968
Since it's in the past tense, I guess you don't do it anymore.

28:23.370 --> 28:24.371
Swimming, I mean.

28:25.873 --> 28:27.174
- What? - Or maybe...

28:28.075 --> 28:29.076
you can't.

28:30.944 --> 28:32.579
Hey, what do you know?

28:32.579 --> 28:34.882
I don't know what it is, but make up your mind soon.

28:35.282 --> 28:36.350
On what?

28:37.518 --> 28:39.720
If you decide to settle here...

28:39.720 --> 28:42.422
or only stay for some fresh air and return to whatever you were doing.

28:43.457 --> 28:45.759
Some resent their failures without committing to anything here,

28:45.759 --> 28:47.528
only to leave after bringing the village down.

28:47.995 --> 28:49.029
I've seen many of them.

28:51.098 --> 28:53.033
Oh, right. I'm just sharing information.

29:03.510 --> 29:04.511
An Na!

29:08.248 --> 29:09.516
Why did you quit your part-time job?

29:09.983 --> 29:11.852
You know who that owner is!

29:13.620 --> 29:14.755
How can I not know?

29:15.322 --> 29:17.424
It's the job you went out of your way to find for your girlfriend,

29:17.424 --> 29:19.293
who lost it after training day and night...

29:19.293 --> 29:21.128
out of guilt for never winning a gold medal for her mom...

29:21.528 --> 29:23.630
before she passed away, only to be forced into retiring.

29:24.264 --> 29:26.033
You said he had ties to the association...

29:26.099 --> 29:28.202
and that he'd let me return even after my years of hiatus!

29:28.202 --> 29:29.403
You know very well!

29:30.370 --> 29:31.805
Yet you did something like that?

29:33.507 --> 29:35.175
Do you really want to ruin your life?

29:36.443 --> 29:37.878
How does everyone say...

29:39.413 --> 29:41.715
that my life has been ruined so easily?

29:43.650 --> 29:45.352
I was your coach for nine years...

29:46.220 --> 29:47.688
and boyfriend for three years.

29:49.323 --> 29:51.758
We've known each other for 12 years, An Na.

29:52.960 --> 29:53.961
Right?

29:55.863 --> 29:57.164
Don't you want to swim again?

29:57.998 --> 30:01.134
Do you want to remain the promising swimmer whose career was ruined...

30:10.777 --> 30:11.778
An Na.

30:12.813 --> 30:14.014
This is my last warning.

30:15.148 --> 30:16.183
Drop the suitcase.

30:18.285 --> 30:19.520
Jerks.

30:20.287 --> 30:21.421
Just you wait.

30:27.361 --> 30:28.529
Where did he go?

31:26.420 --> 31:27.588
I didn't know Parang-ri had...

31:29.423 --> 31:30.824
a sea like this one at the back.

31:37.297 --> 31:38.932
Wait. That's...

32:40.561 --> 32:41.795
Make it or break it.

32:42.763 --> 32:45.566
- Goodness, thank you. - Congratulations.

32:45.566 --> 32:47.100
Everyone, be quiet.

32:47.601 --> 32:49.403
Stop eating and focus.

32:49.870 --> 32:51.805
Daehan Sport University's...

32:52.372 --> 32:53.407
star swimmer,

32:53.974 --> 32:55.375
Ye Gyeong will make a toast for us.

32:59.646 --> 33:02.649
- Star swimmer! - Star swimmer!

33:03.050 --> 33:04.117
I'll begin my toast...

33:05.219 --> 33:07.354
with "Make it or break it."

33:07.921 --> 33:09.122
Make it or break it,

33:09.122 --> 33:11.992
- we're still in our youth! - We're still in our youth!

33:13.861 --> 33:15.362
- You all have to chug. - Okay.

33:16.129 --> 33:18.565
- You drink up, too. - This isn't enough.

33:21.768 --> 33:22.970
Drink up.

33:23.103 --> 33:25.172
The next winner had better think of a toast.

33:27.341 --> 33:30.377
"Make it or break it, we're still in our youth."

33:34.915 --> 33:36.316
But that wasn't the kind of youth...

33:37.050 --> 33:38.218
I experienced.

33:54.701 --> 33:55.869
You must make it to enjoy youth.

34:00.407 --> 34:01.441
But when you're ruined,

34:02.276 --> 34:03.477
you're only left with the blues.

34:14.688 --> 34:17.791
That's why it feels unfair to hear that I'm ruined.

34:19.026 --> 34:20.227
Everyone trained fiercely.

34:21.662 --> 34:22.663
No.

34:23.096 --> 34:24.731
I might have been way fiercer.

34:44.251 --> 34:45.285
What do you want?

34:45.886 --> 34:47.154
How did you find me here?

34:53.193 --> 34:54.595
Teach me how to harvest seafood.

34:58.465 --> 34:59.499
What?

34:59.766 --> 35:01.768
Let's just say you threw the fish heads away.

35:02.169 --> 35:04.204
I'll dive and repay your sea squirts.

35:06.740 --> 35:08.208
It was just something I said.

35:08.442 --> 35:09.443
Don't mind it.

35:11.044 --> 35:12.079
Hey!

35:15.782 --> 35:18.585
You don't just say that someone's life is ruined.

35:19.753 --> 35:20.888
I'm a good swimmer.

35:21.421 --> 35:24.024
I was once on the national youth team.

35:24.958 --> 35:27.027
Just teach me how to do it, and I'll harvest...

35:28.495 --> 35:29.930
the sea squirts and repay you.

35:31.765 --> 35:32.900
So...

35:34.501 --> 35:35.736
teach me...

35:36.803 --> 35:37.838
how to dive and harvest.

35:41.942 --> 35:43.110
I'm not ruined.

35:45.045 --> 35:46.180
Parang-ri Mermaid...

35:46.780 --> 35:47.981
still got her game!

35:59.893 --> 36:01.595
Let him live there for free.

36:03.030 --> 36:04.164
You can live here for free.

36:06.033 --> 36:07.034
I see.

36:07.301 --> 36:08.702
But I still want to pay the rent.

36:10.537 --> 36:12.272
Have a great life here.

36:13.640 --> 36:16.476
You can use either the inner room or the guest room.

36:37.798 --> 36:39.266
She looks like a handful.
